From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/gpu/arm/midgard: fix $(src) normalization on kernels where $(srctree) is the kernel tree

Same root cause as the drivers/base/arm/Kbuild fix in this series:
midgard/Kbuild normalizes $(src) to an absolute path with

    src:=$(if $(patsubst /%,,$(src)),$(srctree)/$(src),$(src))

assuming that when $(src) starts as the relative "." case, prefixing
it with $(srctree) reconstructs this out-of-tree module's own
absolute directory. On Linux v7.2-rc4, $(srctree) resolves to the
KERNEL source tree, not this module's tree, so every downstream use of
$(src) in this file (subdirectory Kbuild includes for arbiter/,
context/, csf/, ipa/, etc., and the -I include paths for platform/ and
base/) resolves to the wrong location. The build fails immediately on
the first subdir include:

    midgard/Kbuild:235: .../kernel-source/./midgard/arbiter/Kbuild: No such file or directory
    make[6]: *** No rule to make target '.../kernel-source/./midgard/arbiter/Kbuild'.  Stop.

$(M) (KBUILD_EXTMOD) is Kbuild's own record of this module's absolute
invocation directory (`make -C $(KDIR) M=<this dir> modules`) and is
correct regardless of $(srctree) semantics -- gpu.mk invokes
`$(MAKE) -C $(GPU_SRC_PATH) ...` where GPU_SRC_PATH =
$(CIX_GPU_PATH)/drivers/gpu/arm, which becomes $(M)/midgard for the
files under midgard/. Fixing this single normalization line (rather
than every individual $(src)/... use site further down the file)
corrects all of them at once, since they all derive from this line.

This is the same fix class already applied and build-verified in this
series for drivers/base/arm/Kbuild (memory_group_manager and
protected_memory_allocator now build cleanly with the equivalent
$(M)-based fix).

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild
+++ b/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild
@@ -18,9 +18,15 @@
 #
 #
 
-# make $(src) as absolute path if it is not already, by prefixing $(srctree)
-# This is to prevent any build issue due to wrong path.
-src:=$(if $(patsubst /%,,$(src)),$(srctree)/$(src),$(src))
+# make $(src) as absolute path if it is not already, by prefixing $(M)
+# (KBUILD_EXTMOD, this out-of-tree module's own absolute invocation
+# directory). $(srctree) is the KERNEL source tree for an external
+# module build, not this module's tree, so prefixing with $(srctree)
+# resolves to the wrong location on kernels where $(src) starts as the
+# relative "." case. $(M) is always this module's own absolute path
+# regardless of kernel version. This is to prevent any build issue due
+# to wrong path.
+src:=$(if $(patsubst /%,,$(src)),$(M)/$(src),$(src))
 
 #
 # Prevent misuse when Kernel configurations are not present by default
